  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nWarmer and drier Wednesday and Thursday as weak high pressure \naloft rebuilds over the interior western US. Moisture from \nwestward-moving hurricanes in the Pacific subtropics should \nstay well to our south. The next upper trough is forecast in \nfrom BC Thursday night and Friday, which is earlier than \nforecast yesterday. As the trough comes closer, southwesterly \nflow aloft may tap into tropical moisture and moisten the cold \nfront now expected in our CWA early Friday. Then after brief \ncooling Friday, next weekend looks sunny and warmer again as \nan upper ridge builds over the western states.",
